    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d751">

                <pb facs="0776" n="518" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg518"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 841.857Ar1/24a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gerard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-08-23T11:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 23, 1915, 11 a. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2105. Please informally inquire of the Foreign Office whether any report has been
                    made to the German Government on the torpedoing and sinking of the British
                    steamship <hi rendition="#italic">Arabic.</hi> Without inviting an explanation
                    you should give Von Jagow an
                    opportunity to explain the attack which we are advised was without warning.
                    Report fully the substance of your conversation.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
